= Henri Becquerel
{c}
{parent=List of physicists}
{title2=1852-1908}
{wiki}

= Antoine Henri Becquerel
{c}
{synonym}

= H. Becquerel
{c}
{synonym}

A <physicist> whose <uranium> experiments helped establish <radioactivity>. His 1896 <photographic plate> tests separated exposure to the material from immediate illumination; the cautious interpretation in his report is part of the story of <Becquerel's uranium-radiation experiment>. He held the chair of applied <physics> at the Paris Museum of Natural History.<Nobel Lectures, Physics 1901–1921/Henri Becquerel - Biographical>[Nobel Lectures, Physics 1901–1921; Biographical identity and professional specialization]{ref}

\Image[https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Henri_Becquerel.jpg]
